The first 0200 surgery attempted to replace all four deprecated
announceForAccessibility(...) consequences with live-region/status values.

Regnet code-first review rejected that design because live regions notify users of
changes to semantic values; they are not a generic repeatable-event broadcaster.
Three existing explicit consequences can repeat while their proposed value remains
byte-for-byte identical:

- Spotify explicit command receipt can repeat while the current playback summary is unchanged.
- The same heartbeat light can be explicitly selected again while its detail text is unchanged.
- Adam can send again in the same mode while a simple "sent" status label is unchanged.

Removing those three legacy calls without a fresh event/status semantic would risk
silently losing a repeated confirmation/detail consequence. That violates the
migration contract and accessibility-first requirement.

The only currently migration-ready consequence is heartbeat automatic material
transition, because the existing announcement identity already represents a material
semantic transition and the owner can use the existing summary value under that exact
gate. Its narrower owner patch is preserved separately.

This file intentionally contains no applyable diff. Git history retains the rejected
attempt for provenance; current source declares it unsafe so future workers cannot
mistake old patch existence for an authorized owner surgery.
